      consumer has to slice headings out of a `body` field, the
      parser has decentralized the format it exists to centralize and
      every consumer becomes a second copy of the body grammar."
    - >-
      "Silently accepting unknown top-level body headings — dropping
      them into a catch-all field, ignoring them, or attaching them to
      the nearest known section. The body vocabulary is closed and
      enumerated; an unknown heading is a `malformed-body` result with
      a reason naming the unknown heading. Silent acceptance lets the
      file format drift open one section at a time while the parser
      pretends the schema is still closed."
    - >-
      "Silently dropping a missing required section instead of returning
      a parse error. If `## Prose`, `## Playbook hub`, or `## Research
