      compose remediation; an MCP-protocol error from a thrown parser
      gives the agent no actionable surface."
    - >-
      "Server-side defaults injected when frontmatter fields or required
      body sections are absent. The user owns the file; if a required
      field is missing, the parser surfaces it as a
      malformed-frontmatter result, and if a required body section is
      missing, the parser surfaces it as a malformed-body result. The
      consumer composes a remediation message. The package never
      silently fills in `name: obsidian`, a default
      `mcpServerConfig.command` of `npx`, or default playbook/research
